<title>CANADA: Sugar rescinds shareholder rights plan.</title>
<headline>Sugar rescinds shareholder rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER, British Columbia 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>BC Sugar Refinery Ltd said late on Tuesday that it will rescind its shareholder rights plan, following the passage of a resolution at its annual shareholders' meeting.</p>
<p>The rights plan would be rescinded at the close of business February 25, the company said.</p>
<p>Earlier on Tuesday, the company reported a first quarter profit of $0.33 per share, down from a $0.44 per share profit in the year-ago quarter.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
